      <p>(C) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;text-decoration:underline;">Preparatory Steps:</b></p>
  <table cellpadding="1">

        <tr style="font-weight:bold; text-align:center;">
      <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:68%;">Preparatory Work</th>
            <th style="width:11%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Check</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">1</td>
            <td>
                Ensure compliance to all MGL Life Saving Rules &amp; COP requirements.
                Conduct Site specific HIRA at site. Ensure all the valves are operating
                correctly and accessible to be operated and in correct position at
                the start of NRO.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
           
            <td align="center">2</td>
            <td>
               Ensure that all the personnel involved in the shutdown operation are briefed regarding the sequence of the operation and are aware of the valve positions., Social distancing, Body temperature, Moitoring periodic hand sanitization, etc.as per GOM guidelines. Ensure availability of adequate quantity of hand sanitizer face mask thermometer etc. for the site team. 
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">3</td>
            <td>
                Ensure No smoking / No Naked flames signs are on site.
                Ensure compliance with all MGL Life Saving Rules and COP requirements.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">4</td>
            <td>
                Ensure that a duly calibrated Gas leak detector and Oxygen meter
                is available on site &amp; are in proper working condition.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">5</td>
            <td>
                Ensure appropriate 5 nos. of fire extinguishers (9 Kgs. each) and
                non-sparking tools are available at Site.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">6</td>
            <td>
                Ensure the fabrication &amp; testing of pipe/valves is completed in
                all respects. <b>Refer COP: Section 051 &amp; 054.</b>
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">7</td>
            <td>
               Ensre all emergency fittings are available at site.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">8</td>
            <td>
                    Ensure lock out and tag out (LOTO) for valves to be closed during
                the NRO. Also ensure application of clamp as suitable before
                operation of valve.
                

            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">9</td>
            <td>
          Ensure proper earthing of the vent hose during the venting operation.
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">10</td>
            <td>
          Switch off TR unit before hot work on Steel Pipeline.
      
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td align="center">11</td>
            <td>
                          
                Ensure that all personnel involved in hot work are with their
                recommended PPE’s.<b> Refer COP: Section 01 (Clause no. 6 –
                Personal Protective Equipment).</b>
                
               
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
      <tr>
            <td align="center">12</td>
            <td>
                 Ensure usage of fire-retardant suits for personnel involved in
                welding and cutting operation.
                
            </td>
            <td align="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
              <tr>
            <td align="center">13</td>
            <td>
                Intimate CNG Stations Mukund Super &amp; Jogeshwari Petrol upply about shutdown in case of Contigency action plan is activated<b>(As per Annexure I)</b>
