        <div  class="title-page">
               <p>(E) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Normal Operation Procedure:</b></p>
              <table>
        <tr>
             <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:68%;">Operation Procedure</th>
            <th style="width:11%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Check</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">1</td>
            <td>
                Ensure compliance with MGL Life Saving rules and COP requirements.
                Conduct site specific HIRA.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">2</td>
            <td>
                Inform Emergency control room about commencement of NRO.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">3</td>
            <td>
                Issue work permit for confined space entry for entering steel valve chambers.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">4</td>
            <td>
                Close the valve V1 (Size 4") completely and OPEN Valve A/G 1 slowly.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">5</td>
            <td>
                Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of Valve V2 and A/G 2.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">6</td>
            <td>
                Connect vent stack and flame arrestor at Valve A/G 2.
                Open A/G 2 and vent the residual gas in the pipeline using a vent stack
                and flame arrestor.
                <br/>
                <b>  Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3 – Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">7</td>
            <td>
                Issue Testing, Commissioning and Purging permit.
                Open Blind of Valve V2 and connect the Nitrogen hose and start
                Nitrogen purging by opening valve V2 and venting from A/G 2
                using a vent stack and flame arrestor.
                <br/>
                <b>  Refer: PTW System</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">8</td>
            <td>
                Check % of gas at A/G 2 &amp; stop nitrogen purging when the level falls below
                the safe limit (Ensure – 0 PPM).
                <br/>
                <b>  Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3 – Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">9</td>
            <td>
                Issue hot and cold work permit, allow the construction to cut the pipe at
                point “A” (Cutting to be done from Hacksaw).
                <br/>
                <b>  Refer: PTW System</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">10</td>
            <td>
                Complete the connectivity of welding of 4" WNRFs (tested WNRF)
                at Point A and fit matching size blind flanges on newly welded flanges
                at the new end of the dia 4" pipe.
            </td>
            <td class="center">Contractor Team</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">11</td>
            <td>
                Ensure quality of joints by reviewing NDT reports of the welds.
                <br/>
                <b> Refer COP: Section 52 (Clause No. 8 – NDT)</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Engineer &amp;
                MGL QA Engineer &amp;
                NDT Agency
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">12</td>
            <td>
                Ensure proper tightening of WNRF-BLRF stud nuts.
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Engineer &amp; <br/>
                MGL QA Engineer
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
           <tr>
            <td class="center">13</td>
            <td>
                Check for any potential sources of ignition around valve V6 and remove if any before venting.
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Technician
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
                     <tr>
            <td class="center">14</td>
            <td>
			Close Valve V2 and put blind flange
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Technician
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
            <tr>
            <td class="center">15</td>
            <td>
			Issue Charging and commissioning permit and then open Valve V1 slowly and start venting from V6 by using vent stack and flame arrestor.
                <b> (Refer: PTW System)</b>
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Technician
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
                  
             <tr>
            <td class="center">16</td>
            <td>
			Continue venting till 95% GIA is achieved at V6 &amp; then close valve V6 and put blind flange.
                <b>(Refer: WI:0 &amp;M WI 102) <br/>Note:</b>
                After termination at Point A, then 4" steel network inside Oschiwara Service Station(CNG station) will be abandon and Valves A/G 1,A/G 2. V6, V7&amp; V8 shall be removed.
            </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Engineer
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>   
               <tr>
            <td class="center">17</td>
            <td>
                Check all flanged joint for leakages with soap solution &amp; Gascoseeker.
			 </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Technician
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>  
               <tr>
            <td class="center">18</td>
            <td>
                Close all work permits and Inform Emergency control room about the completion of NRO </td>
            <td class="center">
                O&amp;M Engineer
            </td>
            <td></td>
        </tr> 
