         <div  class="title-page">
               <p> (G)<b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;"> Contingency Action Plan:</b></p> 
             <p><b style="text-decoration:underline;"> In case of Passing of Valve V1:</b> </p>
         <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="background-color:gray;width:10%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="background-color:gray;width:70%;">Description of work</th>
            <th style="background-color:gray;width:20%;">Responsibility</th>
        </tr>
	<tr>
        <td  style="background-color:gray;" colspan="3">Action Steps in case of Contingency</td>
             </tr>
        <tr>
            <td class="center">1</td>
            <td>
                Give information to Emergency control room about the passing of Valve V1.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">2</td>
            <td>
                Close Valves V11 completely.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">3</td>
            <td>
                Check for potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of Valve V3,
                remove if any. Open valve V3 and start venting the gas using a vent stack
                and flame arrestor in the Pipeline from Valve V3.
                If still gas is found passing, then abandon the NRO and inform the
                emergency control room.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">4</td>
            <td>
                If gas is not passing then carry out the work as per the normal operation
                procedure, ensuring pre and post purging as per the additional valves
                operated sections isolated in conformance with
                COP Section 08 (Clause no. 3 – Purging &amp; commissioning of mains).
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">5</td>
            <td>
                Restore the valves to their original positions as prior to the start of the NRO.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td class="center">6</td>
            <td>
                Inform Emergency Control Room about completion of NRO.
            </td>
            <td class="center">O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
